The results of Johnston [

 5


] on homology manifolds are extended here. It is notpossible to investigate transversality by geometric methods—as in [

 5


] we employbordism and surgery instead.

The proof of transversality is indirect, relying heavily on surgery theory—seeKirby and Siebenmann [

 7


, III, §1], Marin [

 8


] and Quinn [

 11


]. We shall use theformulation in terms of topological block bundles of Rourke and Sanderson [

 12


].

Thus, the surgery exact sequence of [

 1


] does not follow Wall [

 13


] in relatinghomology manifold structures and normal invariants.

(This type of surgery on a Poincaré space is in the tradition of Lowell Jones[

 6


].)
